# Implementation Plan: Enforcing Strict Framework Isolation

This plan updates the architecture to enforce **Strict Framework Isolation** across all supported frameworks: **Django**, **React**, **Vue.js**, **Flutter Desktop**, **Flutter Mobile**, and **WordPress**.

Under Framework Isolation, each framework possesses its own completely self-contained, independent agent structure, automation scripts, pre-commit/post-commit Git hooks, installation scripts, configurations, and documentation inside its dedicated framework folder. Duplication between framework folders is explicitly allowed and preferred over shared cross-framework files.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **Framework Isolation**: Each framework directory (`django/`, `react/`, `vuejs/`, `flutter/desktop/`, `flutter/mobile/`, `wordpress/`) will contain its own self-contained `automation/` directory with independent `setup-project`, `install-hooks`, `pre-commit`, and `post-commit` scripts for both Linux bash (`.sh`) and Windows PowerShell (`.ps1`).
> - **No Centralized Framework Logic**: Root scripts will act strictly as generic entry points / delegators to framework-specific scripts. No framework-specific `if/else` lumping will exist in root hook scripts.
> - **Preserve Context & Features**: All existing agent roles (`*.agent.md`), skills (`SKILL.md`), foundation files (`exampleApi.ts`, `ExampleWidget.tsx`, etc.), and documentation remain completely preserved and updated to reference their own framework's isolated scripts.

